    "value": "Description\n-----------\n\n**ShoppableProduct** is a wrapper content model for a full \"shoppable editorial moment\" — a rendered title, a large image, an optional editorial link, and a presentation choice, plus an ordered list of live SFCC products. It's not just a bare wrapper around the product picker; it covers the whole composed section an editor sees on the page (e.g. the Zimmerse \"Birds in motion\" moment: a heading, a big editorial photo, a \"More\" link, and the product tile next to it).\n\nPer the project's own rule against duplicating commerce data into Contentful, the products themselves are **not modelled by us at all** — the `products` field is provided directly by the **Salesforce Commerce App for Contentful**, which gives editors a live in-editor product/category picker and handles the SKU pointer and storage itself. `title`, `image`, and `link`, by contrast, are ordinary Zimmermann-authored fields — there is no Zimmermann-authored primitive standing in for the *product* itself, only for the editorial framing around it.\n\n**Backs:**\n\n* **Shoppable product caption / product-grid carousel** — the single most consistent pattern across the live-site review (97 of 299 pages, once all three Magento widget names are counted — see 5.9.3a). Confirmed on: [fall-rtw-2026-campaign](https://www.zimmermann.com/fall-rtw-2026-campaign), [accessories-fall-rtw-2026](https://www.zimmermann.com/accessories-fall-rtw-2026), [goldentime-collection](https://www.zimmermann.com/goldentime-collection), the Zimmerse Figma frame (\"Birds in motion\"), and the Runway Pages lookbook grid.\n\nThe `Carousel` presentation variation has not yet been seen in a live example — every sighting so far is either the single static \"Birds in motion\" pairing or the Runway lookbook's `Grid` layout. `Carousel` isn't validated the same way `Grid` is; treat it as provisional until a real example turns up.\n\nScreenshot from Figma\n---------------------\n\n![download](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/486080515/child/attachment/att485130302/download)\n\n*From the*[*Zimmerse Figma frame*](https://www.figma.com/design/QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs/Zimmermann_Designs?node-id=3401-40749)*(\"Birds in motion\" section, node*`3401:55585`*) — the rendered heading (\"Birds in motion,\" what*`title`*holds), the large editorial image (what*`image`*holds), and the product tile itself (MAHON SCARF TIE BIKINI TOP, $850 — what*`products`*resolves via the Salesforce Commerce App). The Runway Pages lookbook shows the underlying product-tile pattern laid out as a grid instead of a carousel.*\n\nConcept of the model design\n---------------------------\n\nnoneShoppableProduct (entry)\ntitle: \"Birds in motion\" (rendered as a heading on the page)\nvariation: Grid (Carousel | Grid — Grid confirmed live, Carousel provisional)\nimage: → image: \"Birds in motion\" editorial photo (optional)\nlink: → link: { label: \"More\", href: \"/story/birds-in-motion\" } (optional)\nproducts: ← Salesforce Commerce App's own picker field (not authored here — live SFCC lookup)\n\nModel fields\n------------\n\n![download](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/486080515/child/attachment/att489816065/download)\n\n| Field | Type | Example |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `title` | Short text — rendered as a heading on the page, centered above the image (per the Zimmerse example) | \"Birds in motion\" |\n| `variation` | Enum: `Carousel` | `Grid` — `Grid` is confirmed live; `Carousel` is provisional (no confirmed sighting yet) | `Grid` |\n| `image` | Reference → `image`, optional — the large editorial image accompanying the shoppable moment | → image: \"Birds in motion\" editorial photo |\n| `link` | Reference → `link`, optional — an editorial CTA/caption link (e.g. \"More\"), separate from anything the product picker provides | → link: `{label: \"More\", href: \"/story/birds-in-motion\"}` |\n| `products` | Field type provided by the **Salesforce Commerce App for Contentful** — not a Zimmermann-authored field. The app owns the picker UI, the live SFCC lookup, and the stored shape | Whatever the app itself stores — see Open items below |\n\nThe React component renders `title` as a visible heading, `image`/`link` as the section's editorial framing, and whatever product data the Salesforce Commerce App resolves for each entry in `products` — name, price, image, and availability all come live from SFCC via the app, never duplicated into Contentful.\n\nOpen items for review\n---------------------\n\n* **No confirmed Carousel-variation example** — only `Grid` (Runway lookbook) and the single-item static case (Zimmerse) are confirmed live/in-design. Hold off building Carousel support until a real example turns up, or confirm directly with the design team.\n* The Zimmerse example also shows a caption line (\"Lana Del Rey in the Rebellion Drawn Sweater in Red/Cream\") alongside the big image — to confirm whether that needs its own text field here, whether it's covered by `link`'s own label, or whether it's a separate Rich Text/Simple Text entry composed alongside this one on the canvas\n* Exactly which field type the Salesforce Commerce App exposes for a multi-product picker (single field vs. an array), and how it's configured against this model — needs checking against the installed app itself\n* Whether a per-product editorial caption override is still needed given products come entirely from the app's own field — if yes, it would need to be a separate, parallel field on this model rather than an attribute of each product\n* Whether `variation` needs the same conditional-field treatment as Media Collection's `indicatorStyle` — no evidence yet either way\n* Model name is provisional"
